// A counterweight drives a belt. Its drum hangs under the roof, joined by an iron shaft, a gear round the corner,
// a shaft down and a gear to a belt along the floor. As the weight falls it turns the train, the belt runs right
// at 1 m/s, and stones dropped on it ride to its end and fall off onto the floor past it. Take the counterweight
// down (E) and nothing drives the train: the belt stops, and a stone dropped on it lies where it lands.
map
################################
################################
#....jjjjjjjjjj*...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#..............j...............#
#.@............*>>>>>>>>>>>....#
################################
end
give Counterweight 1
place 2 2 -8 Counterweight          // its drum under the roof, beside the shaft
expect 3 weights == 1
drop 10 Stone 15 -1
expect 30 turning:20,0 == 1         // the train turns at full speed...
expect 30 supply:20,0 > 0           // ...on the weight's fall
expect 90 ivx:Stone > 3.5           // the belt carries it at ~4 tiles/s (1 m/s)
expect 90 ivx:Stone < 4.5
expect 180 zone:Stone,25,28,-1,0 == 1   // off the end, on the floor past it
expect 180 weighty > 3.3            // the weight has come down a little
saveload 185
expect 186 weights == 1
pickup 190 2 -7                     // take the counterweight down
expect 191 inv:Counterweight == 1
drop 200 Stone 17 -1
expect 300 turning:20,0 == 0        // nothing drives it now
expect 300 zone:Stone,16,18,-2,-1 == 1  // the new stone lies where it landed
